& [P3ICER-001] is exact source preservation and multi-authority lineage
  + [support] raw source, source manifest, processing input manifest, audit, both predecessor implementation authorities, scanner and seal formations, and lower reconciliation evidence are exact
  + [proof_route] immutable hash table, UUID table, signature table, source rehash, and artifact-binding guard

& [P3ICER-002] is evidence-versus-state semantic delineation
  + [support] public names and rustdoc separate evidence label, support lineage, form validity, acquisition, issuance, consumption, and world state
  + [proof_route] semantic review plus static required and forbidden vocabulary assertions

& [P3ICER-003] is Phase3 machine forms profile 0.2
  + [support] PHASE3_MACHINE_FORMS_PROFILE equals cantor-phase3-machine-forms/0.2 exactly
  + [proof_route] direct constant test, serialized form fixture, and static literal assertion

& [P3ICER-004] is exact InventoryConsistencyEvidence enum
  + [support] public closed enum has only NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual and OsSnapshotProven with exact snake_case serde and pure structural validation
  + [proof_route] serialization, deserialization, validation, equality, cardinality, and static no-default/no-alias tests

& [P3ICER-005] is topology forms and receipt profiles 0.3 with scanner unchanged
  + [support] TOPOLOGY_FORMS_PROFILE and TOPOLOGY_RECEIPT_PROFILE equal exact 0.3 values while WINDOWS_TOPOLOGY_PROFILE remains exact 0.1
  + [proof_route] direct constant tests, current receipt fixture, and structural diff

& [P3ICER-006] is exact consistency_evidence receipt field and initial allowed grade
  + [support] required InventoryConsistencyEvidence field replaces consistency in the same semantic position and receipt 0.3 permits only NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + [proof_route] Rust construction, strict JSON round-trip, field-name assertion, valid receipt test, and snapshot negative

& [P3ICER-007] is strict legacy type, field, token, and profile rejection
  + [support] no compatibility alias or migration and all old representations fail explicitly
  + [proof_route] compile/static old-symbol absence plus old profile, field, missing field, dual field, old token, and new-field-old-token negative fixtures

& [P3ICER-008] is preservation of unrelated receipt invariants
  + [support] candidate root, root identity, volume path, admission, digests, nonce, limits, counts, totals, and tick relations remain exact
  + [proof_route] full preexisting topology forms positive and negative suite plus production structural diff

& [P3ICER-009] is reserved OsSnapshotProven rejection without provenance
  + [support] enum structural validation accepts the reserved label while TopologyReceipt 0.3 rejects it with Receipt at consistency_evidence
  + [proof_route] paired enum-positive and receipt-negative tests with exact code, field, and bounded message

& [P3ICER-010] is producer, consumer, and physical authority absence
  + [support] no acquisition, reconciliation conversion, snapshot primitive, issuer, ledger, freshness read, work packet, admission, mutation, or seal behavior
  + [proof_route] public API and static forbidden-surface scan plus zero-effect review

& [P3ICER-011] is safe pure two-module implementation with zero dependency delta
  + [support] production changes only phase3_evidence.rs and topology_forms.rs using safe supplied-value validation
  + [proof_route] Git production diff, Cargo and lockfile byte equality, unsafe/platform/effect scan, build, and audit

& [P3ICER-012] is focused semantic and static proof
  + [support] positive profiles, tokens, round-trip, receipt admissibility, legacy negatives, snapshot rejection, docs, and forbidden compatibility routes are directly exercised
  + [proof_route] focused debug and unique-metadata overflow-checked release unit, integration, static, and evidence tests

& [P3ICER-013] is global quality, audit, recursive evidence, provenance, and rollback closure
  + [support] whole workspace, format, lint, build, docs, dependency, manifest graph, frozen evidence, source hashes, narrative, clean tree, commit, and push all close
  + [proof_route] solution, completion review, proof, evidence manifests, recursive verifier, provenance audit, rollback audit, and publication record

& [P3ICER-014] is valid SJS phase lock and replacement satisfaction signatures
  + [support] every SJS artifact is byte/hash bound and two scoped signatures prospectively supersede the two affected current implementation authorities
  + [proof_route] phase-lock table, canonical signature blocks, registry edges, current evidence signature migration, and post-implementation authority audit

